{"name":"Eliza Jane","hex":"#f4d7dc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"jane","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A silver Genovese coin, first used in England in the 14th century."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Jane, a woman.","Alternative spelling of jean."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jane"}],"entries":[{"title":"Death of Eliza Jane Scovill","blocks":[{"text":"Eliza Jane Scovill was the daughter of AIDS denialist Christine Maggiore, an HIV-positive activist who publicly questioned the link between HIV and AIDS, and supported HIV-positive pregnant women who want to avoid taking anti-HIV medication. Eliza Jane's May 16, 2005 death from AIDS, at the age of three and a half, sparked a social and legal controversy over her mother's decision not to take precautions during pregnancy and breastfeeding to prevent transmission of the virus, and her parents' decision to not have her treated for HIV infection during her life."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Death_of_Eliza_Jane_Scovill"}],"images":[],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Werner's nomenclature of colours greys","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg/500px-Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg","ratio":0.794047619047619,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg","share":0.5425},{"title":"The Jessie and Eliza Jane in Table Bay, Cape of Good Hope, 1829 RMG PY8489","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/The_Jessie_and_Eliza_Jane_in_Table_Bay%2C_Cape_of_Good_Hope%2C_1829_RMG_PY8489.jpg/500px-The_Jessie_and_Eliza_Jane_in_Table_Bay%2C_Cape_of_Good_Hope%2C_1829_RMG_PY8489.jpg","ratio":1.4430665163472378,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Jessie_and_Eliza_Jane_in_Table_Bay,_Cape_of_Good_Hope,_1829_RMG_PY8489.jpg","share":0.4125},{"title":"Eliza Jane LCCN200